perin</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nussinov</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Principles of docking: an overview of search algorithms and a guide to scoring functions</article-title><source>Proteins</source><volume>47</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>409</fpage><lpage>443</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12001221</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp0116-000573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hillisch</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pineda</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilgenfeld</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Utility of homology models in the drug discovery process</article-title><source>Drug Discov Today</source><volume>9</volume><issue>15</issue><fpage>659</fpage><lpage>669</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15279849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0116-000573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Benson</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Lerner</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlson</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Binding MOAD (mother of all databases)</article-title><source>Proteins</source><volume>60</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>340</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15971202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp0116-000573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>B</given-names